Subject: Supply the Mach and memory-pressure sources on Emscripten

Register DISPATCH_SOURCE_TYPE_MACH_RECV and DISPATCH_SOURCE_TYPE_MACH_SEND
(DISPATCH_MACH_SEND_DEAD) sources in the Emscripten event backend over
libmach's watches (<libmach/wait.h>), reached through three functions of
src/mach_emscripten.c (patch 0004), the only file built with Mach headers:
_dispatch_emscripten_mach_watch, _dispatch_emscripten_mach_watch_arm and
_dispatch_emscripten_mach_unwatch. A receive source watches its receive
right or port set for a message; the watch fires once when a message is
queued and is re-armed when the source is resumed, as Darwin's
EVFILT_MACHPORT knote with EV_DISPATCH; a send source watches its send
right for a dead name. libmach calls back with its lock held; the callback
queues the source's muxnote and wakes the manager thread, which merges the
event as the kevent backend does (the receive source's data is
DISPATCH_MACH_RECV_MESSAGE, the send source's DISPATCH_MACH_SEND_DEAD).
DISPATCH_SOURCE_TYPE_MEMORYPRESSURE registers and never fires: a
WebAssembly process has no memory pressure signal. The three source types
are declared available on Emscripten.

